# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The virtualenv is ~6 GB of torch and CUDA, and is fully reproducible from
# pyproject.toml. install.sh rebuilds it.
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# The live config holds the Cider API token. config.example.toml is the
# version that gets committed; the real one never leaves this machine.
config.toml
*.token
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------- large weights
# ~466 MB of downloadable weights. install.sh refetches them.
#
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, `models/` matched *any*
# directory of that name at any depth -- which silently excluded the source
# package `relay/models/` from every commit and every backup for the life of
# this repo. A clone would have installed cleanly and then failed to start on
# `No module named 'relay.models'`. Downloaded weights live outside the repo
# anyway, under ~/.local/share/relay/models.
/models/
*.safetensors

# ------------------------------------------------------------- runtime
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log
screenshots/
sessions/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- backups
# `relay backup` writes here. Explicitly un-ignored, because the whole point
# is that it *is* committed: the wake word was trained on Andrew's voice and
# cannot be downloaded again, and the memory database is not reproducible at
# all. The rules above would otherwise swallow both.
!backup/
!backup/**
# ...but not SQLite's sidecars. They're empty once the snapshot closes, and
# committing them implies the backup depends on files it doesn't.
backup/*.db-wal
backup/*.db-shm
